Complete secret-document sealed enrollment and every custody path; migrate control writers/readers and per-bag effect handling; mint face-bound daemon canon and correct recipe order; remove persona acts from page recipes while preserving proof access; convert carry import to LOAD then MOVE; restore the daemon mirror only after control writers leave; run all five package builds/stamps/typechecks and full suites, Python sensorium suite if its mirrored contract moved, and all relevant e2e review. No commits or pushes were made.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/further-custody-trace`>>

!! Further custody trace

The direct founding route uses `ownedStore`, whose `SealedDocumentStore` deliberately has no bag map, save session, or sealing door. `runFoundTheFace` calls `foundTheFace` without a secret handle or sealed-rest capability. `foundThePlace` creates an empty secret placeholder, but `runInit` persists only the daemon URL in the bootstrap, so that placeholder does not supply a recoverable secret-home address. Enrollment must establish the map and booking before secret writes and preserve the secret address across restart; supplying a bare handle to the existing direct holder would not satisfy sealed rest.

Focused confirmation: <code>pnpm &#45;-filter &#64;lararium/node exec vitest run tests/founding-seed-by-ask.test.ts &#45;-maxWorkers=4</code> failed its one test at `requireSecretHandle` with `secret-home-unavailable`. No implementation change or new ruling followed this trace; items A–G remain open.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/homes-wright-hand-back-commit-72fcb8d9d`>>

!! Homes-Wright hand-back (items B, C, F; D and E went to Terra seats) — commit 72fcb8d9d
* ''B, built:'' one vessel control document, `bags/control` (`mesh/src/control-home.ts`). The daemon document names it, and no recipe composes it. Summons, outcomes, the effect index, receipt facts, ward audits, the mailbox, swarm controls and lease epochs all move there, with every writer and reader. It seals under the lit face (fork 1 in PLACE-RULING).
* ''C, built:'' `bags/daemon-<F>` mints at the face's first worn stand into the face's catalog (`node/src/face-daemon-canon.ts`). The recipe reads working, then the face canon, then kahua, and the daemon document sits beneath every canon (`WikiRecipe.canonBag` plus the `canonUrl` grant). Node only; the browser daemon recipe is unchanged.
* ''F, built:'' both mirrors project again, `wikis/daemon-<F>` and `bags/daemon-<F>`. The placement witness now checks the control families, the daemon mirrors and the control writers, and it reads red on a mutation.
* Remaining reds: node and CLI founding/face tests fail with `secret-home-unavailable` (item A). Two node tests fail from the WIP projector change: foreign-title-projection and projection-standoff-alert. Two CLI tests fail inside carry-verbs (item E).

